    <p style="margin-bottom:20px;">Athens is Limestone County's seat and one of North Alabama's most rapidly evolving communities. The city that once moved at the pace of an agricultural county seat has been transformed by I-65's positioning as a development corridor, the arrival of Mazda Toyota Manufacturing USA, and the influx of residents who have followed the jobs and the quality of life that Limestone County offers. BamaClean has been part of Athens' story since 1993 — from the quieter decades to the current growth wave.</p>
    <p style="margin-bottom:20px;">Athens presents a genuine range of residential cleaning and restoration challenges. The historic neighborhoods around the downtown square and Athens State University have homes built in the 1920s through 1960s with crawlspace foundations, original hardwood floors, and the moisture management challenges that predate modern construction standards. The new subdivisions south of I-65 and along the US-72 corridor represent the other end of the spectrum — rapidly built homes on clay-heavy soil where moisture management and mold risk are factors from the first year of occupancy. We serve both ends of this spectrum with equal competence.</p>
    <p>Limestone County's position in the Tennessee Valley makes it one of the highest-radon-risk counties in North Alabama, a fact that most Athens homeowners don't know. We provide more radon testing in Limestone County than anywhere else in our service area — and we find elevated levels (above the EPA's 4 pCi/L action threshold) in a significant percentage of homes we test. If you've never had your Athens home tested for radon, the data says you should.</p>
  `}
