      <p style="margin-bottom:20px;">Athens and Limestone County sit in the western Tennessee Valley, where flat terrain and agricultural land create open exposure to the severe weather systems that move through North Alabama from the southwest. The county has been struck by significant tornadoes and storm systems multiple times in recent decades — these events create water and structural damage that requires professional restoration, and BamaClean has responded to Athens and Limestone County events repeatedly.</p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:20px;">Limestone County's soil is some of the most moisture-retentive in North Alabama — high clay content that expands and contracts with moisture cycles, shrinks during dry spells, and creates foundation movement and gap formation in homes built on slab and crawlspace foundations alike. These gaps become pathways for moisture intrusion, and the crawlspaces and foundation edges of Athens homes accumulate water during rain events in ways that aren't always visible from inside the home. Mold follows.</p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:20px;">Limestone County has documented elevated radon levels in a significant percentage of tested homes — driven by the uranium-bearing limestone geology that gives the county its name. Radon is produced as uranium in limestone bedrock decays, and that gas migrates upward through soil and foundation into homes. We test more homes for radon in Athens and Limestone County than anywhere else we serve, and we find actionable levels regularly. If you're buying a home in Athens or have lived in one that's never been tested, this is not an abstract risk.</p>
      <p>Pollen season in Limestone County is extended — tree pollen from March through May, grass pollen from May through July, ragweed from August through October — due to the county's agricultural land and its position in the Tennessee Valley. Athens families with allergy sufferers need professional carpet and upholstery cleaning as part of their seasonal health management, not just as periodic aesthetic maintenance.</p>
